# Schedule M-1 Reconciliation — <ENTITY NAME> — FY<YYYY>

**Status**: draft | in-review | final
**Generated**: YYYY-MM-DD

Book-to-tax reconciliation workpaper. See entity-specific sub-skill (`entities/partnership.md`, `entities/s-corp.md`, or `entities/c-corp.md`) for the Schedule M-1 line structure that applies to this entity's return.

## 1. Book Income (starting point)

| | Amount |
|---|---|
| Net income (loss) per books | $ |

## 2. M-1 Adjustments

### Additions (book income lower than taxable income)

| Item | Amount | Permanent / Timing | Authority / Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| Federal income tax expense (C-corp, per books) | $ | Permanent | not deductible |
| Excess of capital losses over capital gains (book) | $ | Timing | limited on return |
| Income recorded on tax return, not on books | $ | Timing | |
| Expenses recorded on books, not deducted on return (e.g., 50% meals, penalties, life insurance premiums where entity is beneficiary) | $ | Permanent | §274, §162(f) |
| Depreciation — book < tax (bonus/§179 acceleration) | $ | Timing | |
| **Total additions** | $ | | |

### Subtractions (book income higher than taxable income)

| Item | Amount | Permanent / Timing | Authority / Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| Income recorded on books, not on return (e.g., tax-exempt interest) | $ | Permanent | §103 |
| Deductions on return, not on books | $ | Timing | |
| Depreciation — tax < book (rare; AMT/ADS convention) | $ | Timing | |
| **Total subtractions** | $ | | |

## 3. Taxable Income (ending point)

| | Amount |
|---|---|
| Book income (line 1) | $ |
| + Total additions | $ |
| − Total subtractions | ($) |
| **Taxable income (loss) per return** | $ |

## 4. Permanent vs. Timing Summary

- Permanent differences (never reverse): list and total — these drive the entity's effective rate away from statutory.
- Timing differences (reverse in future years): list and total — these become next year's beginning M-1 adjustments or deferred tax items.

## Check

- Ending taxable income ties to Form 1120/1065/1120-S taxable income line: yes / **DISCREPANCY** (investigate)
- All timing differences have an offsetting entry logged for the year they reverse: yes / no
- Schedule M-2 (retained earnings / AAA rollforward) ties to this M-1: yes / no / n/a

